Package: rvtr
Type: Package
Title: Relief Visualization for Large Rasters and Mosaics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jens", "Wiesehahn", email = "wiesehahn.jens@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Sky-view factor, positive openness and the archaeological
    Visualization for Archaeological Topography (VAT) blend, following the
    Relief Visualization Toolbox (Kokalj & Somrak 2019). The horizon search
    runs as a fused, OpenMP-parallel C++ kernel, and rasters are processed
    tile by tile so memory use stays bounded regardless of input size. A
    mosaic of many rasters is handled by wrapping it in a GDAL virtual
    raster, so horizon searches read across file boundaries seamlessly and
    tile edges show no seams.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: Rcpp, gdalraster, methods, grDevices
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: GDAL, C++17
